@startuml 04-papeis-repositorio
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

title Repository roles — product vs automation vs artifacts

package "code/\n(runs in target environments)" #E8F4FC {
  package "frontend/" {
    [React app\nSPA] as FE
  }
  package "backend/" {
    [Flask API\nSQLite] as BE
  }
  package "publisher/" {
    [Pi agent\noptional systemd] as PubCode
  }
}

package "scripts/\n(automation: dev, CI, deploy, diagnostics)" #FFF8E8 {
  [deploy-*.sh, test-*.sh,\ndiagnose_*.sh, ...] as Scr
}

package "docs/\n(guides & diagrams)" #F0F0F0 {
  [*.md guides,\ndocs/uml/*.puml] as Doc
}

package "docs/dist/\n(generated — do not edit)" #EEEEEE {
  [svg, pdf] as Dist
}

FE -[hidden]right- BE
BE -[hidden]right- PubCode
Scr ..> FE : build/deploy automation
Scr ..> BE : build/deploy automation
Scr ..> PubCode : optional: sync to Pi
Doc .. Dist : **export-uml-pdf.sh**\nbuilds PDFs from .puml

note right of Scr
  Scripts are **not** the IoT runtime:
  they orchestrate tasks on the dev machine or CI.
end note

note bottom of PubCode
  **Edge** code: runs on the Raspberry / test rig,
  not in the same process as Flask.
end note

@enduml
